=== HINT 1 ===
A C string ends with the null character '\0'.
Walk the pointer (or index) forward until you reach it.

=== HINT 2 ===
You can use a counter:
  int n = 0;
  while (s[n] != '\0') n++;
  return n;

Or pointer arithmetic:
  const char *p = s;
  while (*p) p++;
  return (int)(p - s);

=== HINT 3 (SPOILER) ===
int n = 0;
while (s[n] != '\0') n++;
return n;
